  "status": "Appeal Received",
  "description": "Erection of two-storey rear extensions to No.8 and No.9 Gloucester Square&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-991410d7-7fff-9967-2f39-6ab1405342a8&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;By reason of its size, scale, and positioning, the proposed two-storey rear extension at No.8 Gloucester Square represents an overly large, uncharacteristic, and obtrusive extension that fails to be subordinate to the host dwelling at No.8 Gloucester Square. The extension, therefore, fails to respect the character of the wider terrace and fails to meet policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP17 (Housing design) of The Hackney Local Plan (2020) and policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) and D4 (Delivering good design) of The London Plan (2021) and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025). &lt;/span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
